Source: New York Department of State, Division of Administrative Rules, New York State Constitution editions
(https://dos.ny.gov), and the copy of the January 1, 2022 edition hosted by the New York State Board of Elections
(https://elections.ny.gov); retrieved 2026-11-10.

Constitution and statute text is not copyrightable: under the government edicts doctrine, as the Supreme Court applied
it in Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc., 590 U.S. 255 (2020), no one holds copyright in the laws that legislators
and the people make in their official capacity.

